  "instance_name": "mapping_1",
  "label": "Text implies the visual material represents a historical atrocity remembered only by a specific generation",
  "description": "The text 'only 30's kids will remember this' is mapped onto the visual material of children in concentration camp uniforms behind barbed wire. The text implies that the image depicts a historical event (the Holocaust) that is fading from collective memory, and that only those born in the 1930s (or their children) will remember it. This creates an analogical mapping where the visual material (children in striped uniforms behind barbed wire) is understood as representing a historical atrocity whose memory is being minimized or forgotten by younger generations, as stated in the text.",
